.TH LOCKD 1 "2026-06-23" "lockd 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lockd \- modular security hardening tool for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lockd
[\fB\-\-gui\fR|\fB\-\-cli\fR|\fB\-\-no\-gui\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lockd
applies and audits security hardening measures on Debian and Ubuntu systems
through self\-contained modules grouped into cumulative security levels and
reusable profiles. Privileged actions are performed by a single audited helper
invoked via Polkit.
.PP
With no command and a graphical session available, lockd launches its GTK
interface (provided by the \fBlockd\-gtk\fR package); otherwise it runs the
command\-line interface.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Audit the current security posture of the system.
.TP
.B list
List available hardening modules.
.TP
.B status
Show the state of each module.
.TP
.B enable \fIMODULE\fR
Enable a hardening module.
.TP
.B disable \fIMODULE\fR
Disable a hardening module.
.TP
.B simulate
Show what would change without applying anything.
.TP
.B profile \fIID\fR, profiles
Apply a security profile, or list the available profiles.
.TP
.B level \fIID\fR, levels
Apply a cumulative security level, or list the available levels.
.TP
.B info \fIMODULE\fR
Show detailed information about a module.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Force the graphical interface.
.TP
.B \-\-cli, \-\-no\-gui
Force the command\-line interface.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve and report actions without modifying the system.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/lockd/modules
Hardening module catalogue and scripts.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/lockd/profiles
Security profile definitions.
.TP
.I /var/lib/lockd/journal.jsonl
Append\-only journal of privileged operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1)
